      {
        "id": 122858,
        "name": "bluedarky",
        "username": "bluedarky",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/bluedarky/{size}/1975_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-12-15T01:29:15.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Sefirit\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/s/e68b1a/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Sefirit:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div><b>Pydro wrote:</b><br><blockquote>Originally, that line was in every fowl card, but it caused problems with some mechanics, like Hair Trigger Reflexes. For the new edition, thry took the line off the birds and put it on Matty. However, the over-sized card is from the old version. So, if 6ou used the new cards with the over-sized card, that text was lost.\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote></div>\nThe funny thing is that Hair trigger is in the SAME expansion. &nbsp;How that issue was never considered while that expansion was being designed or during playtesting is quite surprising to me.\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>The same way some broken combos end up in the same set block in MtG I'd assume, just an oversight.</p>\n<p>Also remember that the original Rook City would have had far less playtesters than the more recent expansions.</p>",
        "post_number": 21,
        "post_type": 1,
