      {
        "id": 122861,
        "name": "Mezike",
        "username": "Mezike",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/m/c6cbf5/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2014-12-15T12:32:22.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"arenson9\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/arenson9/48/1900_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> arenson9:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I think towards the beginning there was more general acceptance that as long as you had fun playing, it didn't really matter so much how some of the arcane interactions worked. If it comes up while playing, make a decision and move on.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>I still do. Life is too short to worry about whether or not you played an obscure card interaction correctly in a co-operative game  <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/slightly_smiling_face.png?v=12\" title=\":slightly_smiling_face:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":slightly_smiling_face:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>",
