      {
        "id": 122862,
        "name": "Silverleaf",
        "username": "Silverleaf",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/silverleaf/{size}/2332_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-12-15T14:27:33.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Mezike\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/m/c6cbf5/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Mezike:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<div><b>arenson9 wrote:</b><br><blockquote>I think towards the beginning there was more general acceptance that as long as you had fun playing, it didn't really matter so much how some of the arcane interactions worked. If it comes up while playing, make a decision and move on.</blockquote></div>\n&nbsp;I still do. Life is too short to worry about whether or not you played an obscure card interaction correctly in a co-operative game  :slightly_smiling_face: <span>\n</span></blockquote>\n</aside>\n\n<p><span>Unfortunately I have this overwhelming (probably obsessive) desire to be right. I do make a quick \"just for now\" ruling but I have to find out for sure as well as I can for next time.</span></p>",
